      "final_text": "Done. `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\n**Fix:** [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean) now defines `sqrt` as the deployed loop with the PR-4486 correction \u2014 returning the smaller of the last two iterates (`minInt`) instead of the last iterate `z`. This turns the sometimes-rounded-up result into the floor root.\n\n**Proof sketch:** the loop is Newton's method for `Nat.sqrt (a * 10^10)` from seed `a/2 + 5\u00b710^9`. I showed the seed is above the root, every iterate stays above it and in decimal range (so nothing reverts), the error at least halves each step (error \u2264 `2^(167-n) + 2`, so \u2264 3 after 167 steps), one quadratic step then lands in `{root, root+1}`, which is stable \u2014 so after 256 iterations the two final iterates straddle the root and their minimum is exactly the floor. All 5 theorems hold with the locked statements, accepted by all 6 kernels with only the permitted axioms, and the executable passes all 2001 property cases.\n\nPassport: `.proofforge/passport-002.json` (`94bd7ac6\u2026`).",
